" prescription painkillers are called opioids, which are opium-like "
"compounds. They are manufactured to react on the nervous system in the same "
"way as drugs derived from the opium poppy, like heroin. The most commonly "
"abused opioid painkillers include oxycodone, hydrocodone, meperidine, "
"hydromorphone and propoxyphene."
msgstr ""

